{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Jacob saw that there was grain in Egypt.</b> As it is said: ״The eye sees and the ear hears — HaShem made both of them.״ Why say thus? Did the Holy One, blessed be He, not make the entire body? Rather, all the other limbs are destined to give an accounting, except for the eye and the ear. And why? Because the eye sees against its will, and so too the ear — unlike the rest of the limbs. And Rabbi said: וירא יעקב — come and see: Jacob, an old man, sitting in his house, and he sees what there is in Egypt, while his ten sons go in and out and do not see. And even though Jacob and his sons were prophets beforehand, and Joseph was no farther from them than a journey of four or five days, they did not know where he was. And also Joseph — why did he not inform his father that he was in Egypt? Because they imposed a ban of excommunication among themselves, and also they stipulated with the Holy One, blessed be He, and Joseph too they swore not to reveal. And the verse proves it, as it is written: ״Have every man go out from me״ — he did not want to reveal it to strangers because of the oath. Some explain: when he was a slave he did not want to tell him, for it would only pain him more, and likewise when he was in prison. And even when he was king, he would not believe him, for even at the end when his brothers told him, he did not believe them, as it is written: ״his heart went numb, for he did not believe them.״ And furthermore, if he had told his father, he feared lest his brothers hear and panic and flee, this one northward and that one southward, out of great fear that he would kill them — and so his father would grieve over them, and it would cause great distress to his father. Therefore he waited until his brothers came to him, and he revealed himself to them first, and appeased them with words, that he held nothing against them, and told them to tell their father that he rules over the entire land of Egypt."], :book :genesis, 